KZ3 patch 2101 (RSX pass 96): the GPU adapter on one log line, and runtime setters for the mouse options.

libs/video/rsx_d3d12_device.h: rsx_adapter_line (pure; host test tools/smoke/test_d3d12_warp.sh) formats
"[rsx] D3D12 adapter: <DXGI description> (vendor 0x10DE NVIDIA device 0x....), <dedicated MB> MB, hardware|software
(WARP)" and rsx_d3d12_log_device prints it once per process next to the existing "[d3d12] device" line, so the release
support package's facts.txt (tools/release/support.py GPU_RX: adapter ... vendor name) finds the GPU.

libs/input/pad_mouse.{h,c}: pad_mouse_opts_set/get change the user sensitivity, the zoom factor and invert Y at run
time (the next look update uses them); pure clamp/step/format helpers (0.5..10 in steps of 0.5) and
pad_mouse_ini_upsert (set one key under [input] in kz3.ini text, other lines byte for byte) for the Options > Mouse
page in port/kz3/main.cpp. Host test tools/smoke/test_mouse_opts.sh.

